  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The educated present: -",
   "texto": [
    "In the dictionary the verbs end up in **-다**: To speak, it is removed and added **-아요** or **-어요**. It's the educated form of every day.",
    "In the regular verbs, if the last vowel of the root is **ㅏ** or **ㅗ**, add **-아요**:",
    "With any other vowel, **-어요**: There are some irregular changes that you will learn with your examples.",
    "**하다** verbs make **해요**.",
    "La gran ventaja: el verbo **no cambia con la persona**. 가요 es «voy», «vas», «va», «vamos»… y también sirve para preguntar."
   ]
  },
